          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structure on a category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+graded+algebras"} differential graded algebras
            or more specifically on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+differential+graded-commutative+algebras"} category of differential graded-commutative algebras
            tends to present an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-algebra+over+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-algebraic+theory"} ∞-algebras
          %p
            For dg-algebras bounded in negative or positive degrees, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+Dold-Kan+correspondence"} monoidal Dold-Kan correspondence
            asserts that their model category structures are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalent
            to the corresponding
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+algebras"} model structure on (co)simplicial algebras
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
          %p
            The case of model structures on unbounded dg-algebras may be thought of as induced from this by passage to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+geometry"} derived geometry
            modeled on formal duals of the bounded dg-algebras. This is described at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-geometry"} dg-geometry
          %h2#general General
          %p
            The category of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+chain+complexes"} category of chain complexes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+monoids+in+a+monoidal+model+category"} model structure on monoids in a monoidal model category
            apply.
          %p
            Below we spell out special cases, such as restricting to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoids"} commutative monoids
            when working over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+zero"} characteristic zero
          %h2#on_connective_dgcalgebras On connective dgc-algebras
          %p
            We discuss the projective model structure on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+graded-commutative+algebras"} differential non-negatively graded-commutative algebras
            %a{:href => "#BousfieldGugenheim76"} Bousfield-Gugenheim 76
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            for
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dennis+Sullivan"} Dennis Sullivan
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
          %h3#definition Definition
          #dgcCochainAlgebrasInNonNegativeDegrees.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+zero"} characteristic zero
            #eq:CategoryOfdgcAlgebras.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi dgcAlg
                      %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Categories
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    dgcAlg^{\geq 0}_{k}
                    \\;\in\;
                    Categories
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+unital+algebra"} unital
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+graded-commutative+algebras"} differential graded-commutative algebras
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              in non-negative degrees, equivalently the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoids"} commutative monoids
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ch
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ch^{\geq 0}(k)
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochain+complexes"} cochain complexes
              in non-negative degrees, equipped with the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+chain+complexes"} tensor product of chain complexes
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#GelfandManin96"}> Gelfand-Manin 96, V.3.1
            )
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial
                and
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            %p
              In
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi dgcAlg
                      %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dgcAlg^{\geq 0}_{k}
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:CategoryOfdgcAlgebras"} (1)
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
                  is the ground field algebra
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
                  is the zero algebra
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
                  (which is indeed a unital algebra).
          %p
            (Beware that this is incorrectly stated in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#GelfandManin96"} Gelfand-Manin 96, p. 335
          %p More generally:
          .num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
                and
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
            %p
              In
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi dgcAlg
                      %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dgcAlg^{\geq 0}_{k}
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:CategoryOfdgcAlgebras"} (1)
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
                  is given by the
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+algebras"} tensor product of algebras
                %p
                  (see at
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %em
                      %a{:href => "category+of+monoids#PushoutOfCommutativeMonoids"} pushouts of commutative monoids
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
                  is given by
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
                  on
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+spaces"} graded vector spaces
                %p
                  (since the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
                  is a
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
          #dgcCochainAlgebraInNonNegDegreeOfFiniteType.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              %strong (finite type)
            %p
              Say that a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dgc-algebra"} dgc-algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %msubsup
                      %mi dgcAlg
                      %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in dgcAlg^{\geq 0}_k
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#dgcCochainAlgebrasInNonNegativeDegrees"}
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+type"} finite type
              if its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
              is in each degree of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
              as a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
          #ProjectiveModelStructureOnCdgAlg.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              %strong (projective model structure on rational connective dgc-algebras)
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi dgcAlg
                      %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (dgcAlg^{\geq 0}_k)_{proj}
              for the catgory of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dgc-algebras"} dgc-algebras
              from def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#dgcCochainAlgebrasInNonNegativeDegrees"}
              equipped with the following
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classes"} classes
              of morphisms:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalences"} weak equivalences
                  are the
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphism
              %li
                %p
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrations"} fibrations
                  are the degreewise
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjections"} surjections
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#BousfieldGugenheim76"}> Bousfield-Gugenheim 76, Def. 4.2
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#GelfandManin96"} Gelfand-Manin 96, Def. V.3.3
          #IndeedProjectiveModelStructureOnCdgAlg.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi dgcAlg
                      %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (dgcAlg^{\geq 0}_k)_{proj}
              from def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProjectiveModelStructureOnCdgAlg"}
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              = succeed "." do
                %em projective model structure
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#BousfieldGugenheim76"}> Bousfield-Gugenheim 76, Theorem 4.3
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#GelfandManin96"} Gelfand-Manin 96, Theorem V.3.4
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"}> category of fibrant objects
                )
            %p
              Evidently every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi dgcAlg
                      %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (dgcAlg^{\geq 0}_k)_{proj}
              (Def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProjectiveModelStructureOnCdgAlg"}
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#IndeedProjectiveModelStructureOnCdgAlg"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+object"} fibrant object
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} category of fibrant objects
          %p
            The nature of the cofibrations is discussed
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#SullivanAlgebras"} below
          %h3#properties Properties
          %h4#SullivanAlgebras Cofibrations and Sullivan algebras
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              %strong (sphere and disk algebras)
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k[n]
              for the graded vector space which is the ground field
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              in degree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              and 0 in all other degrees. For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semifree+dgc-algebras"} semifree dgc-algebras
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S(n) \coloneqq (\wedge^\bullet k[n], 0)
            %p
              and for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 1
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semifree+dgc-algebras"} semifree dgc-algebras
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi n
                              %mo =
                              %mn 0
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msup
                                %mo ∧
                                %mo •
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi k
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                              %mo ⊕
                              %mi k
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ,
                              %mn 0
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi n
                              %mo &gt;
                              %mn 0
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    D(n)
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\left\lbrace
                    \\array{
                    0 &amp; (n = 0)
                    \\\
                    (\wedge^\bullet (k[n] \oplus k[n-1]), 0) &amp; (n \gt 0)
                    }
                    \\right.
            %p
              for which the differential sends the generator of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k[n-1]
              to that of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k[n]
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    i_n \colon S(n) \to D(n)
            %p
              for the obvious morphism that takes the generator in degree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              to the generator in degree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              (and for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 0
              it is the unique morphism from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (0,0)
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \gt 0
              write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    j_n \colon k[0] \to D(n)
                    \\,.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (generating cofibrations)
            %p The sets
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    I = \{i_n \}_{n \geq 1} \cup \{k[0] \to S(0), S(0) \to k[0]\}
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo &gt;
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    J = \{j_n \}_{n \gt 1}
            %p
              are sets of generating cofibrations and acyclic cofibrations, respectively, exhibiting the model category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi dgcAlg
                      %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (dgcAlg^{\geq 0}_k)_{proj}
              from prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#IndeedProjectiveModelStructureOnCdgAlg"}
              as a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated model category
          %p
            review includes (
            %a{:href => "#Hess06"}> Hess 06, p. 6
            )
          %p
            In this section we describe the cofibrations in the model structure on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi dgcalg
                    %mi k
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi proj
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (dgcalg^{\geq 0}_k)_{proj}
            (def.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProjectiveModelStructureOnCdgAlg"}
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#IndeedProjectiveModelStructureOnCdgAlg"}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+Dold-Kan+correspondence"} monoidal Dold-Kan correspondence
          %p Before we characterize the cofibrations, first some notation.
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} graded vector space
            write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo •
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge^\bullet V
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmann+algebra"} Grassmann algebra
            over it. Equipped with the trivial differential
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 0
            this is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semifree+dga"} semifree dga
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\wedge^\bullet V, d=0)
          %p
            With
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            our ground field we write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (k,0)
            for the corresponding dg-algebra, the tensor unit for the standard
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal structure
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dgAlg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dgAlg
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmann+algebra"} Grassmann algebra
            on the 0-vector space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (k,0) = (\wedge^\bullet 0, 0)
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              %strong (Sullivan algebras)
            %p
              A
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+Sullivan+algebra"} relative Sullivan algebra
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              of dg-algebras that is an inclusion
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi k
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (A,d) \to (A \otimes_k \wedge^\bullet V, d')
            %p
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,d)
              some dg-algebra and for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              some graded vector space, such that
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  there is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well+ordered+set"} well ordered set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi J
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              %li
                %p
                  indexing a basis
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mi α
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi α
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi J
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{v_\alpha \in V| \alpha \in J\}
                  of
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi V
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              %li
                %p
                  such that with
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mrow
                            %mo &lt;
                            %mi β
                        %mo =
                        %mi span
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi α
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi β
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_{\lt \beta} = span(v_\alpha | \alpha \lt \beta)
                  for all basis elements
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mi β
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_\beta
                  we have that
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo ′
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mi β
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi A
                        %mo ⊗
                        %msup
                          %mo ∧
                          %mo •
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mrow
                            %mo &lt;
                            %mi β
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        d' v_\beta \in A \otimes \wedge^\bullet V_{\lt \beta}
                        \\,.
            %p
              This is called a
              %strong minimal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+Sullivan+algebra"} relative Sullivan algebra
              if in addition the condition
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi α
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi deg
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi α
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi deg
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\alpha \lt \beta) \Rightarrow (deg v_\alpha  \leq deg v_\beta)
            %p
              holds. For a Sullivan algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (k,0) \to (\wedge^\bullet V, d)
              relative to the tensor unit we call the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semifree+dga"} semifree dga
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\wedge^\bullet V,d)
              simply a
              = succeed "." do
                %strong Sullivan algebra
              %strong minimal Sullivan algebra
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (k,0) \to (\wedge^\bullet V, d)
              is a minimal relative Sullivan algebra.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              Sullivan algebras were introduced by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dennis+Sullivan"} Dennis Sullivan
              in his development of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
                \-algebras)
            %p
              Because they are
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semifree+dgas"} semifree dgas
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\wedge^\bullet V,d)
              are (at least for degreewise finite dimensional
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E-algebra"} L-∞-algebra
            %p
              The co-commutative differential co-algebra encoding the corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E-algebra"} L-∞-algebra
              is the free cocommutative algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo ∨
                      %mo •
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vee^\bullet V^*
              on the degreewise dual of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              with differential
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi d
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D = d^*
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∨
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∨
                    %mi ⋯
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\omega(D(v_1 \vee v_2 \vee \cdots v_n)) =
                    \- (d \omega) (v_1, v_2, \cdots,  v_n)
            %p
              for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega \in V
              and all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi V
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_i \in V^*
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (cofibrations are relative Sullivan algebras)
            %p
              The cofibrations in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi dgcAlg
                      %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (dgcAlg^{\geq 0}_{k})_{proj}
              are precisely the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retracts"} retracts
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+Sullivan+algebras"} relative Sullivan algebras
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi k
                      %msup
                        %mo ∧
                        %mo •
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %mi d
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,d) \to (A\otimes_k \wedge^\bullet V, d')
            %p
              Accordingly, the cofibrant objects in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi dgcAlg
                      %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (dgcAlg^{\geq 0}_{k})_{proj}
              are precisely the Sullivan algebras
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
