              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+power"} pullback power
              with respect to the simplicial
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+space"} mapping space
              functor (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MappingSpaceSimOndgcCochainAlgebrasInNonNegDegrees"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Maps
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi W
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Maps
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %munder
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mi Maps
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi V
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Maps
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi W
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    p^i
                    \\;\colon\;
                    Maps(W,X)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    Maps(V,X)
                    \\underset{Maps(V,Y)}{\times}
                    Maps(W,Y)
            %p is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibration"} Kan fibration
                  if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                  is a cofibration and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                  a fibration in the projective
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
                  structure from prop.
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#IndeedProjectiveModelStructureOnCdgAlg"}
              %li
                %p
                  in addition a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
                  (i.e. a weak equivalence in the
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                  or
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                  is a weak equivalence in the projective model structure from prop.
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#IndeedProjectiveModelStructureOnCdgAlg"}
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#BousfieldGugenheim76"}> Bousfield-Gugenheim 76, prop. 5.3
            )
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_5 Remark
            %p
              Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PoweringOfdgcCchainAlgebrasInNonNegativeDegreeOverFiniteSimplicialSets"}
              %em would
              say that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi dgcAlg
                      %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (dgcAlg^{\geq 0}_k)_{proj}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
              with respect to the simplicial enrichment from def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MappingSpaceSimOndgcCochainAlgebrasInNonNegDegrees"}
              were it not for the fact that prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PoweringOfdgcCchainAlgebrasInNonNegativeDegreeOverFiniteSimplicialSets"}
              gives the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/powering"} powering
              only over finite simplicial sets.
          %h4#relation_to_simplicial_sets Relation to simplicial sets
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction+between+simplicial+sets+and+connective+dgc-algebras"}> Quillen adjunction between simplicial sets and connective dgc-algebras
                )
            %p
              The
              = succeed "-construction" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PL+de+Rham+complex"} PL de Rham complex
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              in a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
              between
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+model+structure"} opposite
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+model+structure+on+connective+dgc-algebras"} projective model structure on connective dgc-algebras
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi DiffGradedCommAlgebras
                      %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mi proj
                      %mi op
                    %munderover
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊥
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mi Qu
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi exp
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Ω
                            %mi PLdR
                            %mo •
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi SimplicialSets
                      %mi Qu
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\big(
                    DiffGradedCommAlgebras^{\geq 0}_{k}
                    \\big)^{op}_{proj}
                    \\underoverset
                    {
                    \\underset
                    {\;\;\; exp \;\;\;}
                    {\longrightarrow}
                    }
                    {
                    \\overset
                    {\;\;\;\Omega^\bullet_{PLdR}\;\;\;}
                    {\longleftarrow}
                    }
                    {\bot_{\mathrlap{Qu}}}
                    SimplicialSets_{Qu}
          %h4#relation_to_cosimplicial_commutative_algbras Relation to cosimplicial commutative algbras
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+Dold-Kan+correspondence"} monoidal Dold-Kan correspondence
            gives a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+cosimplicial+algebras"} projective model structure on cosimplicial commutative algebras
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi cAlg
                      %mi k
                      %mi Δ
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (cAlg_k^{\Delta})_{proj}
          %h4#PreservationOfWeakEquivalencesUnderPushout Preservation of weak equivalences under pushout
          #PushoutAlongRelativeSullivanModelsPreservesQuasiIsos.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_7 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
                along
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+Sullivan+models"} relative Sullivan models
                preserves
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphisms"} quasi-isomorphisms
            %p
              In the projective model structure on connective dgc-algebras (Def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProjectiveModelStructureOnCdgAlg"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
              along a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+Sullivan+model"} relative Sullivan model
              preserves weak equivalences (quasi-isomorphisms).
          %p
            This is
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#FelixHalperinThomas00"} Felix-Halperin-Thomas 00, Lemma 14.2, using Prop. 6.7 (ii)
          %p
            The same statement for augmented dgc-algebras is in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Baues88"} Baues 88, Section I.8, Lemma 8.16
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_6 Remark
            %p
              Lemma 14.2 in
              %a{:href => "#FelixHalperinThomas00"} Felix-Halperin-Thomas 00
              is stated under the additional assumption that the dgc-algebras being pushed put have
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi H
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^0(-) = k
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_7 Remark
            %p
              Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PushoutAlongRelativeSullivanModelsPreservesQuasiIsos"}
              comes close to saying that the projective model structure on connective dgc-algebras is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+proper+model+category"} left proper model category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrations"} cofibrations
              is larger than that of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+Sullivan+algebras"} relative Sullivan algebras
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retracts"} retracts
              (see e.g
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#Hess06"} Hess 06
          %h4#change_of_scalars Change of scalars
          %p
          #ExtensionOfScalarsQuillenAdjunction.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+zero"} characteristic zero
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi i
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q} \xhookrightarrow{i} k
              the corresponding inclusion of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension+of+scalars"} extension of scalars
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \;\dashv\;
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/restriction+of+scalars"} restriction of scalars
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi dgcAlg
                      %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mi proj
                    %munderover
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊥
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mi Qu
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi res
                            %mi ℚ
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %msub
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi ℚ
                          %mi k
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi dgcAlg
                      %mi ℚ
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\big(
                    dgcAlg^{\geq 0}_k
                    \\big)_{proj}
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{res_{\mathbb{Q}}}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{ (-) \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} k }{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\bot_{\mathrlap{Qu}}}
                    \\big(
                    dgcAlg^{\geq 0}_{\mathbb{Q}}
                    \\big)_{proj}
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
              between the respective projective model categories (Def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProjectiveModelStructureOnCdgAlg"}
            %p
          (
          %a{:href => "#BousfieldGugenheim76"}> Bousfield &amp; Gugenheim 1976, Lemma 11.6
          )
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              It is immediate that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/restriction+of+scalars"} restriction of scalars
              is a
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+Quillen+functor"} right Quillen functor
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  It preserves
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrations"} fibrations
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjections"} surjections
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
              %li
                %p
                  It preserves
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalences"} weak equivalences
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
                  on
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochain+cohomology"} cochain cohomology
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+groups"} groups
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochain+complexes"} cochain complexes
            %p
          %h4#CommVsNoncomm Commutative vs. non-commutative dg-algebras
          %blockquote
            %p this needs harmonization
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_8 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %msub
                      %mi dgcAlg
                      %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi dgAlg
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F dgcAlg_k \to dgAlg_k
            %p
              from (graded-)commutative
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              part of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ab
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi dgAlg
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ←
                    %mi CdgAlg
                    %mo :
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Ab
                    \\colon
                    dgAlg
                    \\stackrel{\leftarrow}{\to}
                    CdgAlg
                    \:
                    F
          %blockquote
            %p boundedness?
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The forgetful functor clearly preserves fibrations and cofibrations. It has a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ab
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              to its quotient
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A/[A,A]
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              Let the ground
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+zero"} characteristic zero
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              which has the structure of an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+an+operad"} algebra over
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-k-operad"} E-∞ operad
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
              morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to A_c
              to a commutative dg-algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_c
              which is
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a morphism of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-k-operad"} E-∞ algebras
                  (where
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi c
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_c
                  has the obvious
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-k-operad"} E-∞ algebras
                  structure)
              %li
                %p
                  a weak weak equivalence in the model structure on dg-algebras (i.e. a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphism
                  of the underlying cochain complexes).
          %p
            This is in (
            %a{:href => "#KrizMay95"}> Kriz-May 95, II.1.5
            ).
          %p So this says that the weak equivalence classes of the commutative dg-algebras in the model category of all dg-algebras already exhaust the most general non-commutative but homotopy-commutative dg-algebras.
          #HomotopyFaithfulnessOfforgettingCommutativity.num_remark
            %h6#remark_8 Remark
            %p
              Discussion of a restricted kind of homotopy-faithfulness of the forgetful functor from the homotopy theory of commutative to not-necessarily commutative dg-algebras is in (
              %a{:href => "#Amrani14"}> Amrani 14
              ).
          %h2#Unbounded Unbounded dg-algebras
          %p
            We discuss now the case of unbounded dg-algebras. For these there is no longer the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+Dold-Kan+correspondence"} monoidal Dold-Kan correspondence
            available. Instead, these can be understood as arising naturally as function
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+geometry"} derived
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-geometry"} dg-geometry
            over formal duals of bounded dg-algebras, see
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+algebras+on+%E2%88%9E-stacks"} function algebras on ∞-stacks
          %h3#GradingsAndConventions Gradings and conventions
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+geometry"} derived geometry
            two categorical gradings interact: a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive
            = succeed "-groupoid" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
