                  \\mathcal{O}(X_1)_0 \oplus \mathcal{O}(X_2)_{-1} \oplus
                  \\mathcal{O}(X_3)_{-2} \oplus \cdots
                  \\\
                  \\uparrow^{d}
                  \\\
                  \\mathcal{O}(X_0)_0 \oplus \mathcal{O}(X_1)_{-1} \oplus
                  \\mathcal{O}(X_2)_{-2} \oplus \cdots
                  \\\
                  \\uparrow^{d}
                  \\\
                  \\mathcal{O}(X_0)_{-1} \oplus \mathcal{O}(X_1)_{-2} \oplus
                  \\mathcal{O}(X_2)_{-3}\oplus \cdots
                  \\\
                  \\uparrow^{d}
                  \\\
                  \\vdots
                  }
                  \\right)
                  \\,.
          %h3#ForUnboundedDGAlgebrasDefinition Definition
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic"} characteristic
              0 let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi cdgAlg
                    %mo =
                    %mi CMon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    cdgAlg = CMon(Ch_\bullet(k))
            %p
              be the category of undounded commutative dg-algebras. With fibrations the degreewise surjections and weak equivalences the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphisms"} quasi-isomorphisms
              this is a
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            %p which is
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+model+category"}> proper
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"}> combinatorial
                  \.
          %p
            The existence of the model structure follows from the general discussion at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-algebras+over+an+operad"} model structure on dg-algebras over an operad
          %p
            Properness and combinatoriality is discussed in (
            %a{:href => "#ToenVezzosi"}> ToënVezzosi
            ):
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                in lemma 2.3.1.1 they state that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi cdgAlg
                        %mo +
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cdgAlg_+
                constitutes the first two items in a triple which they call an
                %em HA context
                \.
            %li
              %p this implies their assumption 1.1.0.4 which asserts properness and combinatoriality
          %p
            Discussion of cofibrations in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi dgAlg
                    %mi proj
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dgAlg_{proj}
            is in (
            %a{:href => "#Keller"}> Keller
            ).
          %h3#properties_2 Properties
          %h4#Properness Properness
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi cdgAg
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cdgAg_k
            be the projective model structure on commutative unbounded dg-algebras from above.
          %p
            This is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+model+category"} proper model category
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/q/204414/381"} here
          %h4#derived_tensor_product Derived tensor product
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi cdgAg
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cdgAg_k
            be the projective model structure on commutative unbounded dg-algebras from above
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_9 Proposition
            %p
              For cofibrant
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi cdgAlg
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in cdgAlg_k
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi k
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A\otimes_k (-) : k Mod \to A Mod
            %p
              preserves
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphism
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi cdgAlg
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A,B \in cdgAlg_k
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k Mod
              coincides in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
              with the derived
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
              in
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mi Mod
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k Mod
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %munderover
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi k
                      %mi L
                    %mi B
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %msubsup
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi k
                      %mi L
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A \coprod_k^{L} B \stackrel{}{\to} A \otimes_k^L B
            %p
              is an isomorphism in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ho
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mi Mod
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(k Mod)
          %p
            This follows by the above with (
            %a{:href => "#ToenVezzosi"}> ToënVezzosi, assumption 1.1.0.4, and page 8
            ).
          %h4#SimplicialHomObjects Derived hom-functor
          %p
            The model structure on unbounded dg-algebras is
            %em almost
            a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
            %em
              %a{:href => "model+structure+on+dg-algebras+over+an+operad#SimplicialEnrichment"} simplicial enrichment
            at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-algebras+over+an+operad"} model structure on dg-algebras over an operad
            for details.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_9 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic"} characteristic
              0. Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi poly
                      %mo •
                    %mo :
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi cdgAlg
                      %mi k
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet_{poly} : sSet \to (cdgAlg_k)^{op}
              be the functor that assigns polynomial
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms+on+simplices"} differential forms on simplices
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi dgcAlg
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A,B \in dgcAlg_k
              define the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi cdgAlg
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ↦
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi cdgAlg
                          %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi k
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi poly
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    cdgAlg_k(A,B) : ([n] \mapsto Hom_{cdgAlg_k}(A, B \otimes_k \Omega^\bullet_{poly}(\Delta[n]))
                    \\,.
            %p This extends to a functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi cdgAlg
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msubsup
                      %mi cdgAlg
                      %mi k
                      %mi op
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi cdgAlg
                      %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %mi sSet
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    cdgAlg_k(-,-) : cdgAlg_k^{op} \times cdgAlg_k \to sSet
                    \\,.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_10 Proposition
            %p
              The functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi cdgAlg
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cdgAlg_k(-,-)
              satisfies the dual of the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout-product+axiom"} pushout-product axiom
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i : A \to B
              any cofibration in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi cdgAlg
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cdgAlg_k
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : X \to Y
              any fibration, the canonical morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi cdgalg
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi cdgAlg
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi cdgAlg
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi cdgAlg
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (i^*, p_*) : cdgalg_k(A,B) \to
                    cdgAlg_k(A,X)
                    \\times_{cdgAlg_k(A,Y)} cdgAlg_k(B,Y)
            %p
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibration"} Kan fibration
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              or
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              is.
          %p
            This implies in particular that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            cofibrant,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi cdgAlg
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cdgAlg_k(A,B)
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
          %p
            The proof works along the lines of (
            %a{:href => "#BousfieldGugenheim76"}> Bousfield-Gugenheim 76, prop. 5.3
            ). See also the discussion at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-algebras+over+an+operad"} model structure on dg-algebras over an operad
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p We give the proof for a special case. The general case is analogous.
            %p
              We show that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              cofibrant, and for any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              (automatically fibrant),
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi cdgAlg
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cdgAlg_k(A,B)
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            %p
              By a standard fact in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
              (due to
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#BousfieldGugenheim76"} Bousfield-Gugenheim 76
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms+on+simplices"} differential forms on simplices
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi poly
                      %mo •
                    %mo :
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi cdgAlg
                      %mi k
                      %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet_{poly} : sSet \to (cdgAlg^+_k)^{op}
              is a left
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen functor
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
            %p
              Specifically for each
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horn"} horn
              inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Λ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi k
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda[n]_k \hookrightarrow \Delta[n]
              we have that the restriction map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi poly
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi poly
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Λ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet_{poly}(\Delta[n]) \to \Omega^\bullet_{poly}(\Lambda[n]_k)
              is an acyclic fibration in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi cdgAlg
                        %mi k
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cdgAlg_k^*
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi cdgAlg
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cdgAlg_k
            %p
              A
              = succeed "-horn" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi cdgAlg
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cdgAlg_k(A,B)
              is a morphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                      %mo ⊗
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi poly
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Λ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B \otimes \Omega^\bullet_{poly}(\Lambda[n]_k)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              in
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                            %mo ⊗
                            %msubsup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mi poly
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi σ
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                            %mo ⊗
                            %msubsup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mi poly
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Λ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi n
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                              %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; B \otimes \Omega^\bullet_{poly}(\Delta[n])
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{\sigma}}\nearrow &amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    A &amp;\to&amp; B \otimes \Omega^\bullet_{poly}(\Lambda[n]_k)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is cofibrant, then such a lift does always exist.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_11 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi cdgAlg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in cdgAlg
              cofibrant,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi cdgAlg
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cdgAlg_k(A,B)
              is the correct
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+hom-space"} derived hom-space
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi cdgAlg
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    cdgAlg_k(A,B)
                    \\simeq
                    \\mathbb{R}Hom(A,B)
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              By the assumption that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is cofibrant and according to the facts discussed at
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+hom-space"} derived hom-space
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mi B
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi k
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi poly
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    s B : [n] \mapsto B\otimes_k \Omega^\bullet_{poly}(\Delta[n])
            %p
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+resolution"} resolution
              %em simplicial frame
              for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi cdgAlg
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cdgAlg_k
            %p
              Since polynomial differential forms are acyclic on simplices (discussed
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://nlab.mathforge.org/nlab/show/differential+forms+on+simplices"} here
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi const
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi s
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    const B \to s B
            %p
              is degreewise a weak equivalence. It remains to show that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s A
              is fibrant in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+model+structure"} Reedy model structure
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi cdgAlg
                        %mi k
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi Reedy
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, cdgAlg_k]_{Reedy}
            %p One finds that the matching object is given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi match
                    %mi s
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi k
                    %mo =
                    %mi B
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi poly
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (match s B)_k = B \otimes \Omega^\bullet_{poly}(\partial \Delta[k])
                    \\,.
            %p
              Therefore
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s B
              is Reedy fibrant if in each degree the morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi match
                    %mi s
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi poly
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (s B_k \to (match s B)_k ) = (\Omega^\bullet_{poly}(\partial \Delta[k] \hookrightarrow \Delta[k]))
            %p
              is a fibration. But this follows from the fact that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi poly
                      %mo •
                    %mo :
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo →
                    %msubsup
                      %mi cdgAlg
                      %mi k
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet_{poly} : sSet \to cdgAlg_k^{op}
              is a left
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen functor
              (as discussed at
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms+on+simplices"} differential forms on simplices
          %h4#DerivedCopowering
            Derived copowering over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi sSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
          %p
            We discuss a concrete model for the
            = succeed "-copowering" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi cdgAlg
                    %mi k
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∘
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (cdgAlg_k)^\circ
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            in terms of an operation of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi cdgAlg
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cdgAlg_k
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
          %p First notice a basic fact about ordinary commutative algebras.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_12 Proposition
            %p
              In
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi CAlg
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CAlg_k
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              is given by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
              over
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi A
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi i
                                    %mi A
                            %mtd
                              %mi A
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                              %mi B
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo ←
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi i
                                    %mi B
                            %mtd
                              %mi B
                      %mo )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi A
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi Id
                                    %mi A
                                  %msub
                                    %mo ⊗
                                    %mi k
                                  %msub
                                    %mi e
                                    %mi B
                            %mtd
                              %mi A
                              %msub
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi k
                              %mi B
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo ←
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi e
                                    %mi A
                                  %mo ⊗
                                  %msub
                                    %mi Id
                                    %mi B
                            %mtd
                              %mi B
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    A
                    \&amp;\stackrel{i_A}{\to}&amp;
                    A \coprod B
                    \&amp;\stackrel{i_B}{\leftarrow}&amp;
                    B
                    }
                    \\right)
                    \\simeq
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    A
                    \&amp;\stackrel{Id_A \otimes_k e_B}{\to}&amp;
                    A \otimes_k B
                    \&amp; \stackrel{e_A \otimes Id_B}{\leftarrow}&amp;
                    B
                    }
                    \\right)
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              We check the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
              of the coproduct: for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi CAlg
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \in CAlg_k
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g : A,B \to C
              two morphisms, we need to show that there is a unique morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi k
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f,g) : A \otimes_k B \to C
              such that the diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi Id
                                  %mi A
                                %mo ⊗
                                %msub
                                  %mi e
                                  %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                            %msub
                              %mo ⊗
                              %mi k
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ←
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi e
                                  %mi A
                                %mo ⊗
                                %msub
                                  %mi Id
                                  %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mi g
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↙
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi g
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A
                    \&amp;\stackrel{Id_A \otimes e_B}{\to}&amp;
                    A \otimes_k B
                    \&amp;\stackrel{e_A \otimes Id_B}{\leftarrow}&amp;
                    B
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{f}}\searrow &amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{(f,g)}} &amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{g}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; C
                    }
            %p
              commutes. For the left triangle to commute we need that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f,g)
              sends elements of the form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a,e_B)
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(a)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f,g)
              sends elements of the form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (e_A, b)
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g(b)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi k
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \otimes_k B
              is a product of two elements of this form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (a,b) = (a,e_B) \cdot (e_A, b)
            %p
              this already uniquely determines
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f,g)
              to be given on elements by the map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (a,b) \mapsto f(a) \cdot g(b)
                    \\,.
            %p
              That this is indeed an
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              are
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_9 Remark
            %p For these derivations it is crucial that we are working with commutative algebras.
          .num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              We have that the
              = succeed "ing" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copower"} copower
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              with the map of sets from two points to the single point
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi A
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi k
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi μ
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (* \coprod * \to *) \cdot A
                    \\simeq
                    (
                    A \otimes_k A
                    \\stackrel{\mu}{\to}
                    A
                    )
            %p
              is the product morphism on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi A
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mi A
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\emptyset \to *)\cdot A
                    \\simeq
                    (k \stackrel{e_A}{\to} A)
            %p
              is the unit morphism on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : S \to T
              any map of sets we have that the tensoring
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi f
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (S \stackrel{f}{\to} T) \cdot A
                    \=
                    A^{\otimes_k |S|}
                    \\to
                    A^{\otimes_k |T|}
            %p
              is the morphism between
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+power"} tensor power
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              of the cardinalities of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              on the right corresponding to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \in T
              is the iterated product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^{\otimes_k |f^{-1}\{t\}|} \to A
              on as many tensor powers of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              as there are elements in the preimage of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
              under
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
          %p
            The analogous statements hold true with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi CAlg
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CAlg_k
            replaced by
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi cdgAlg
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cdgAlg_k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi sSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in sSet
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi cdgAlg
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in cdgAlg_k
            we obtain a simplicial cdg-algebra
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∈
                  %msubsup
                    %mi cdgAlg
                    %mi k
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S \cdot A \in cdgAlg_k^{\Delta^{op}}
          %p
            by the ordinary degreewise
            = succeed "ing" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copower"} copower
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi cdgAlg
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cdgAlg_k
            has coproducts (equal to the tensor product over
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %p This is equivalently a commutative monoid in simplicial unbounded chain complexes
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi cdgAlg
                    %mi k
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi op
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi CMon
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  cdgAlg_k^{\Delta^{op}} \simeq CMon(Ch^\bullet(k)^{\Delta^{op}})
                  \\,.
          %p
            By the logic of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+Dold-Kan+correspondence"} monoidal Dold-Kan correspondence
            the symmetric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+monoidal+functor"} lax monoidal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moore+complex"} Moore complex
            functor (via the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Zilber+map"} Eilenberg-Zilber map
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            in non-positively graded cochain complexes in unbounded cochain complexes
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi CMon
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo −
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C^\bullet(S \cdot A) \in CMon(Ch^\bullet_-(Ch^\bullet(k)))
                  \\,.
          %p
            Since the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+complex"} total complex
            functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Tot
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tot : Ch^\bullet(Ch^\bullet(k)) \to Ch^\bullet(k)
            is itself symmetric lax monoidal (…), this finally yields
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Tot
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi CMon
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi cdgAlg
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Tot C^\bullet(S \cdot A) \in CMon(Ch^\bullet(k)) \simeq
                  cdgAlg_k
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_10 Definition
            %p Define the functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CC
                    %mo :
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo ×
                    %mi cdgAlg
                    %mo →
                    %mi cdgAlg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    CC : sSet \times cdgAlg \to cdgAlg
            %p by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CC
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mi Tot
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    CC(S,A) := Tot C^\bullet(S \cdot A)
                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_10 Remark
            %p We have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CC
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %msub
                          %mi Y
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    CC(Y,A)^n := \bigoplus_{k \geq 0} (A^{\otimes_k |Y_k| })_{n+k}
          %p
            This appears essentially (…) as (
            %a{:href => "#GinotTradlerZeinalian"}> GinotTradlerZeinalian, def 3.1.1
            ).
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_13 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-limit"} (∞,1)-copowering
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi dgcAlg
                      %mi k
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∘
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (dgcAlg_k)^\circ
              over
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
              is modeled by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi CC
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CC
          %p
            This follows from (
            %a{:href => "#GinotTradlerZeinalian"}> GinotTradlerZeinalian, theorem 4.2.7
            ), which asserts that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
            of this tensoring is the unique
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
            = succeed "-copowering." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_14 Proposition
            %p The functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CC
                    %mo :
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi cdgAlg
                      %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi cdgAlg
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    CC : sSet \times cdgAlg_k \to cdgAlg_k
            %p preserves weak equivalences in both arguments.
          %p
            This is essentially due to (
            %a{:href => "#Pirashvili"}> Pirashvili
            ). The full statement is (
            %a{:href => "#GinotTradlerZeinalian"}> GinotTradlerZeinalian, prop. 4.2.1
            ).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_11 Remark
            %p
              This means that the assumption for the copowering models of higher order
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hochschild+cohomology"} Hochschild cohomology
              are satsified in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi cdgAlg
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cdgAlg_k
              which are described in the section
              %a{:href => "http://nlab.mathforge.org/nlab/show/Hochschild+cohomology#PirashviliHigherOrder"} Pirashvili's higher Hochschild homology
              is satisfied:
            %p
              this means that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi cdgAlg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in cdgAlg
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi sSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in sSet
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CC
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CC(S,A)
              is a model for the function
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+loop+space+object"} free loop space object
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spec
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec A
              %a{:href => "http://nlab.mathforge.org/nlab/show/Hochschild+cohomology#OvercdgAlgs"} Higher order Hochschild homology modeled on cdg-algebras
              for more details.
          %h4#DerivedPowering
            Derived powering over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi sSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
          .num_prop
            %h6#claim Claim
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ∈
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in \infty Grpd
              be presented by a degreewise finite
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
              (which we denote by the same symbol).
            %p
              Then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limit"} homotopy limit
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi cdgAlg
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cdgAlg_k
              over the
              = succeed "-shaped" do
