            For every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectrum"} ring spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            there is the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+spectra"} algebra spectra
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mi H
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R := H \mathbb{Z}
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+spectrum"} Eilenberg-MacLane spectrum
            for the
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integer"} integer
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \mathbb{Z}
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_16 Proposition
            %p
              There is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
              between the standard
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              structure for
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi H
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \mathbb{Z}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+spectra"} algebra spectra
              and the model structure on unbounded differential graded algebras.
          %p
            See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+spectrum"} algebra spectrum
            for details.
          %h4#RelationToEInfinityAlgebras
            Relation to
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔼
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{E}_\infty
          %p
            Commutative dg-algebras over a field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            of characteristic 0 constitute a presentation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-infinity+algebras"} E-infinity algebras
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            ([Lurie, prop. A.7.1.4.11]).
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+equivariant+dgc-algebras"} model structure on equivariant dgc-algebras
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+differential+graded-commutative+superalgebras"} model structure on differential graded-commutative superalgebras
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+chain+complexes"} model structure on chain complexes
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-modules"} model structure on dg-modules
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-operads"} model structure on dg-operads
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-algebras+over+an+operad"} model structure on dg-algebras over an operad
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %strong model structure on dg-algebras
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-categories"} model structure on dg-categories
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-coalgebras"} model structure on dg-coalgebras
          %h2#references References
          %h3#on_connective_dgcalgebras_2 On connective dgc-algebras
          %p
            The cofibrantly generated model structure on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+graded-commutative+algebras"} differential graded-commutative algebras
            is originally due to
          %ul
            %li#BousfieldGugenheim76
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aldridge+Bousfield"}> Aldridge Bousfield
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Gugenheim"} Victor Gugenheim
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/On+PL+deRham+theory+and+rational+homotopy+type"} On PL deRham theory and rational homotopy type
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/memo-8-179"} ams:memo-8-179
          %p Textbook account:
          %ul
            %li#GelfandManin96
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergei+Gelfand"}> Sergei Gelfand
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yuri+Manin"} Yuri Manin
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Methods+of+homological+algebra"} Methods of homological algebra
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-662-12492-5"} doi:10.1007/978-3-662-12492-5
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li#Hess06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kathryn+Hess"}> Kathryn Hess
                , p. 6 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Rational homotopy theory: a brief introduction
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "https://jdc.math.uwo.ca/summerschool/"} Summer School on Interactions between Homotopy Theory and Algebra
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.AT/0604626"} arXiv:math.AT/0604626
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Christensen"} Dan Christensen
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Dwyer"} William Dwyer
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Mandell"} Michael Mandell
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brooke+Shipley"} Brooke Shipley
                (eds.),
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Interactions between Homotopy Theory and Algebra
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1090/conm/436"} doi:10.1090/conm/436
            %li#Moerman15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joshua+Moerman"}> Joshua Moerman
                , Section II of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Rational Homotopy Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.ru.nl/publish/pages/813282/rational_homotopy_theory.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/MoermanRationalHomotopyTheory.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The approach in
            %a{:href => "#Hess06"} Hess 06
            makes use of the general discussion in section 3 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Goerss"}> Paul Goerss
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kirsten+Schemmerhorn"} Kirsten Schemmerhorn
              = succeed "," do
                %em Model categories and simplicial methods
              = succeed "," do
                %em Interactions between Homotopy Theory and Algebra
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.AT/0609537"} arXiv:math.AT/0609537
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1090/conm/436"} doi:10.1090/conm/436
          %p
            that obtains the model structure from the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+chain+complexes"} model structure on chain complexes
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li#Baues88
              %p
                Baues, Chapter I.8 of:
                %em Algebraic Homotopy
                (
                %a{:href => "https://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~v1ranick/papers/baues4.pdf"} pdf
            %li#FelixHalperinThomas00
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yves+F%C3%A9lix"}> Yves Félix
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+Halperin"} Stephen Halperin
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Claude+Thomas"} Jean-Claude Thomas
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Rational Homotopy Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4613-0105-9"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4613-0105-9
          %p
            Generalization to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+rational+homotopy+theory"} equivariant rational homotopy theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Laura+Scull"}> Laura Scull
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A model category structure for equivariant algebraic models
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/S0002-9947-07-04421-2"} doi:10.1090/S0002-9947-07-04421-2
          %h3#on_noncommutative_dgalgebras On non-commutative dg-algebras
          %p
            For general
            %strong non-commutative
            (or rather: not necessarily graded-commutative) dg-algebras a model structure is given in
          %ul
            %li#Jardine97
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+F.+Jardine"}> J. F. Jardine
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/JardineModelDG.pdf", :title => "A Closed Model Structure for Differential Graded Algebras"} A Closed Model Structure for Differential Graded Algebras
          %p This is also the structure used in
          %ul
            %li
              J. L Castiglioni, G. Cortiñas,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Cosimplicial versus DG-rings: a version of the Dold-Kan correspondence
              %strong 191
              (2004) 119-142 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0306289"}> arXiv:math/0306289
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jpaa.2003.11.009"} doi:10.1016/j.jpaa.2003.11.009
          %p
            where aspects of its relation to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+cosimplicial+rings"} model structure on cosimplicial rings
            is discussed. (See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+Dold-Kan+correspondence"} monoidal Dold-Kan correspondence
            for more on this).
          %h3#on_unbounded_dgalgebras On unbounded dg-algebras
          %p Discussion of the model structure on unbounded dg-algebras over a field of characteristic 0 is in
          %ul
            %li#ToenVezzosi
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bertrand+To%C3%ABn"}> Bertrand Toën
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gabriele+Vezzosi"} Gabriele Vezzosi
              %em HAG II, geometric stacks and applicatons
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0404373v4"}> arXiv:math/0404373v4
              )
          %p A general discussion of algebras over an operad in unbounded chain complexes is in
          %ul
            %li#Hinich
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Hinich"}> Vladimir Hinich
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Homological algebra of homotopy algebras
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/q-alg/9702015"} arXiv:q-alg/9702015
              %em Erratum
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0309453"}> arXiv:math/0309453
              ))
          %p
            A survey of some useful facts with an eye towards
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-geometry"} dg-geometry
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Behrend
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kai+Behrend"}> Kai Behrend
              ,
              %em Differential graded schemes I: prefect resolving algebras
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0212225"}> arXiv:0212225
              )
          %p Discussion of cofibrations in unbounded dg-algebras are in
          %ul
            %li#Keller
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bernhard+Keller"}> Bernhard Keller
              ,
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\infty
                \-algebras, modules and functor categories
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.jussieu.fr/~keller/publ/ainffun.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %h3#more More
          %p
            The derived copowering of unbounded commutative dg-algebras over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi sSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
            is discussed (somewhat implicitly) in
          %ul
            %li#GinotTradlerZeinalian
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gr%C3%A9gory+Ginot"}> Grégory Ginot
              , Thomas Tradler, Mahmoud Zeinalian,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Derived higher Hochschild homology, topological chiral homology and factorization algebras
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1011.6483"} arxiv/1011.6483
          %p
            The
            %em commutative
            product on the dg-algebra of the higher order Hochschild complex is discussed in
          %ul#GinotTradlerZeinalianChenModel
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gr%C3%A9gory+Ginot"}> Grégory Ginot
              , Thomas Tradler, Mahmoud Zeinalian,
              %em A Chen model for mapping spaces and the surface product
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/PS_cache/arxiv/pdf/0905/0905.2231v1.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            The relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-infinity+algebras"} E-infinity algebras
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#KrizMay95
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Kriz"} Igor Kriz
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
                %em Operads, algebras, modules and motives
                , Astérisque No 233 (1995)
            %li#Lurie
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
                , section 7.1 of
                %em Higher algebra
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.harvard.edu/~lurie/papers/higheralgebra.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p The relation between commutative and non-commutative dgas is further discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Amrani14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ilias+Amrani"}> Ilias Amrani
                ,
                %em Comparing commutative and associative unbounded differential graded algebras over Q from homotopical point of view
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1401.7285"}> arXiv:1401.7285
                )
            %li#Amrani14b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ilias+Amrani"}> Ilias Amrani
                ,
                %em Rational homotopy theory of function spaces and Hochschild cohomology
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1406.6269"}> arXiv:1406.6269
                )
          %p
            For more see also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-algebras+over+an+operad"} model structure on dg-algebras over an operad
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limits"} homotopy limits
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+colimits"} homotopy colimits
            of dg-algebras is in
          %ul
            %li#Walter06
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ben+Walter"}> Ben Walter
              ,
              %em Rational Homotopy Calculus of Functors
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0603336"}> arXiv:math/0603336
              )
        .revisedby
          %p
